cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "snakemake_scstseq: a Snakemake workflow for single-cell (Xenium) and spot-level (Visium) spatial transcriptomics"
abstract: >-
  A Snakemake workflow for spatial transcriptomics that reads 10x Genomics
  Xenium (single-cell, imaging-based) and Visium (spot-level, sequencing-based)
  vendor output directories and produces per-section QC with platform-specific
  thresholds, normalization, clustering and marker genes (scanpy), a spatial
  neighbors graph with neighborhood enrichment and Moran's I spatially variable
  genes (squidpy), and a self-contained cross-sample HTML report. Containerized
  with Docker and Apptainer.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Ji"
    family-names: "Wang"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3443-5857"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gynecoloji/snakemake_scstseq"
url: "https://github.com/gynecoloji/snakemake_scstseq"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - Xenium
  - Visium
  - Snakemake
  - scanpy
  - squidpy
  - quality control
  - spatially variable genes
  - bioinformatics workflow
